{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
  "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:19 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So if the -- there were a State law that said you must disclose anything that could reasonably be viewed as a conflict of interest, then -- then you would lose?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Generally speaking, contractual duties have a consequence of paying damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In other words, Mr. Weyhrauch -- Mr. Weyhrauch sent a solicitation letter, and that's about the size of it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: One of your arguments -- an important argument in your brief is the -- the Federal balance, apart from vagueness for a moment --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Let me ask you right at that point: Does the prohibited action, namely, voting -- does that vote have to be contrary to -- serve the interest of the other party?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But I don\u2019t mean them to be comical. Look, think of a person who is really angry at his employer and he changes all the direction signs around in the building to mislead him so that the employer will miss the key meeting and make the wrong decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Before McNally, there was a body of case law that made very clear that there was a substratum fiduciary duty -- and I\u2019ll limit this to the public official context for now, because that\u2019s the most critical and important context. If you look at the common law in every State, public officials are fiduciaries. The core obligation of a fiduciary is the duty of loyalty, the duty not to advance your personal interests at the expense of the government who you serve."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why didn't Congress say that instead of -- instead of -- of setting up this mush of language that doesn't even mention McNally, does not use a phrase that any opinion pre-McNally used? That -- that phrase does not appear, as I understand, it in any of the cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Yes, but you say that in order for the violation to be complete, he must follow up by voting in the interest of the company rather than the polls?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ayer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. AYER: Thank you, Your Honor. I have four quick points I'd like to make. The first one is that McNally is a case -- there were issues about the jury instructions, but the basic fact pattern was clear. It was a kickback scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: You're saying that you\u2019ll win on the facts, not the theory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ayer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0003-0005",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Secondly, he voted; when he voted he actually ended up voting twice on the bill in a form that -- that VECO didn't want."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the proposition advanced by the United States, that honest services may be proved by establishing that a public official knowingly concealed a conflict of interest"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1196",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e1910c5fd31dca322e6426eed5a1e9fbdd02a1ff2aee997bf3f0cdae750c310a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e1910c5fd31d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
